# tools/ales_stereo_compress_env_witness.rish — stereo_compress_env: the attack/release compressor carried into stereo, the linked envelope driving one linked gain over time (ALES161).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES161.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-065200_fill-ales161-lotus-stereo-compress-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_envelope.rye (ALES160 — the linked envelope, its stereo_env_step reused whole), lotus/stereo_compress.rye (ALES157 — the linked gain this drives over time, its memoryless form the unit-coefficient
# limit), lotus/compress_env.rye (ALES53 — the mono attack/release compressor, its CompressEnvError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/compress.rye (ALES50 — the softened ceiling),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max).
#
# lotus/stereo_compress_env.rye compresses a span of sample-PAIRS in a master above a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one gain reduction following the shared LINKED envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared
# envelope toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES160's step (attack while rising, release while falling): within the threshold both pass byte for byte, above it the softened target comp = threshold +
# excess·den/num (ALES50's ceiling on the linked envelope) yields one gain comp/e applied to both raw samples — one detector, one gain, the image held. CompressEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused
# whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the instantaneous law (unit attack and release reducing it to ALES157's memoryless stereo_compress byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's
# zero-smoothing limit is exactly the memoryless one already proven), the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with left' equal to ALES53's mono compress_env(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the
# independent per-channel compress_env differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase), the knob laws (unit ratio the identity, a slower attack letting
# the transient through), the carry law (a span in two pieces equal to the whole once on both), and the sub-threshold/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_compress_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-compress-env: Language EN — stereo_compress_env compresses a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master above a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one gain reduction following the shared linked envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail), the attack fraction while it rises and the release while it falls; where the smoothed envelope sits within the threshold both channels pass byte for byte, and where it rises above, the envelope's excess is softened by the ratio and the single gain (the softened target over the envelope) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the threshold, ratio, attack, release, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never compresses one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope across calls, so a span compressed in two pieces equals the whole once."
say "ales-stereo-compress-env: Style Radiant — ALES157's stereo_compress leans on a pair the instant it sees it: a peak the moment it arrives is already softened, and the softening vanishes the moment the peak passes. A real compressor breathes — it hears a peak arrive and leans in over a few samples (the attack), then eases the gain back as the sound falls away (the release). ALES160 built exactly that breath for stereo, one shared envelope tracking the linked peak, and proved it once. This rung spends both proofs: it drives the gain reduction from the smoothed linked envelope rather than the bare pair, and applies the one resulting gain to both channels — a compressor that leans in patiently and lets go gently, the image held to the sample the whole time. Two proofs fused: the detector is linked and time-smoothed (the louder channel deciding the shared loudness over time), and the gain is linked (one softened gain from the linked envelope applied to both, since compressing each channel by its own envelope would smooth and soften on different samples and pump the image). The crux is six laws: the instantaneous law (unit attack and release making the linked envelope the instantaneous linked peak, so this equals ALES157's memoryless stereo_compress byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit exactly the memoryless one already proven); the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES53's mono compress_env of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel compress_env genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, a slower attack letting more of a transient through, monotone); the carry law (a span compressed in two pieces equal to compressing the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the sub-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked envelope never crosses the threshold passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-compress-env: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the envelope step (ALES160's proven stereo_env_step) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the softened target at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain comp over e in the half-open interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a compressor writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the threshold, ratio, both coefficients, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never compresses one channel and leaves the other torn; the linked envelope is asserted a legal magnitude in zero to sample_max each sample and the softened target within threshold to envelope, so the single gain is a genuine reduction; StereoCompressEnvError is ALES53's CompressEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The instantaneous law is proven by running both stereo_compress_env under unit attack and release and ALES157's memoryless stereo_compress on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gain-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES53's mono compress_env of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono compress_env of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere and a slower attack letting the first onset sample through where an instant attack clamps it; the carry law proves a span compressed in two pieces equal to the whole once on both channels; and the sub-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove a below-threshold master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction, the attack and release fractions per sample index, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_compress_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_compress_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-compress-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_compress_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-compress-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-compress-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-compress-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-compress-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-compress-env line"
